r"""apply_decisions_v32.py -- record the three warmstart decisions of 2026-10-10 and pin the
warmstart by hash.

    python apply_decisions_v32.py --root . --dry-run
    python apply_decisions_v32.py --root .
    python verify_decisions_v32.py --root .
    python src\record_warmstart_v3.py --gate results\g4_v3m

The decisions (DATASET_V3_SPEC V3-10, V3-12, §12 items 1, 2, 14, 15):
  * Suite C (sink_50) at its natural share (18.6% of the training weight), as G4 v3m trained;
  * early stopping on the unweighted contested validation accuracy, as G4 v3m trained;
  * warmstart = results\g4_v3m\student_2001.pt, by G4 delivery (+0.044 pp over student_2000,
    ahead in 12 of 14 cells).
Nothing is retrained and no code-signature module is touched: data\v3m, data\phaseB_v3m and
results\g4_v3m stay valid.

NEW
  src/record_warmstart_v3.py     applies the selection rule to a passed gate's students and
                                 writes <gate>/warmstart.json once: the decision, the rule,
                                 the evidence and every candidate's sha256 (the checkpoints
                                 are not in git); --check verifies a checkpoint or a backup
                                 copy; selected_checkpoint() is how M5 loads the warmstart.
DOCS
  docs/DATASET_V3_SPEC.md        status; V3-10 and V3-12 decided; §10 step 8 results and step 9;
                                 §12 items 1, 2 and 14 closed, item 15 (the warmstart) added.
  docs/CLAUDE.md                 status: the warmstart and how to load it.
  results/README.md              v32 note; rows for student_eval_val/test.json and
                                 warmstart.json.

Assertion-guarded str.replace, as docs/CLAUDE.md requires: every anchor must match exactly
once, all edits are staged in memory, nothing is written unless every anchor in every file
matches. A file whose guard string is present is skipped (idempotent). Reads with universal
newlines, writes LF.
"""
import argparse
import io
import os
import sys

